{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792162540,"nonce":"x7j/5l2GwuhB6hsr/X8a1VpcNbM=","title":"Expose a cheap version check on Signal\u003cT\u003e for change detection without a clone","message":"A consumer with an expensive decode step per read (ashui's SignalString,\ncaching a UTF-8 string into a Haxe String) needs to know whether a signal's\nvalue changed since it last looked, without paying for `get`/`try_get`'s\nvalue clone and without registering a dependency (dependency registration\nstays on a separate tracked read, so the two concerns don't couple).\n\n`SignalNode` already carries a `version: u64` bumped on every `set`, and\n`ReactiveGraph::signal_version` already reads it, untracked. Added\n`Signal\u003cT\u003e::version() -\u003e Option\u003cu64\u003e`, mirroring `try_get`'s in-flight-graph\nfast path so a derived or effect can call it mid-computation without\nre-locking the mutex its own evaluation is already holding.","files":null}]}